WEBVTT

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.700
Okay, I'm off.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.200
Take care.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.850
Oh. Morning, Sis.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:14.860
Mornin'.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.190
You're going out even earlier than usual.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.090
You got practice?

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.520
Yeah. The new first-years have come in,
so it's a busy time for the captain.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.540
How many first-years do you have?

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.350
Five so far.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.510
They're all from Nanyou Lions and they're on
sports scholarships, so they're pretty good.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.220
Wow, really?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.300
That club's famous!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.470
And it looks like Nanyou's
coach is joining us, too.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.540
The coach, too? Wow, that's great news.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.950
As an OG, I was worried 
after what happened...

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.440
But I guess the school hasn't
forgotten about the baseball team.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:51.910
Yeah.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.640
I see.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.640
Keep it up, Daigo!

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.870
You're responsible for Fuurin 
Middle School's baseball team now!

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.120
Uh, Sis... you're in high school now.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.500
You'll catch cold walking around like that.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.100
Oh, my!

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.960
I'm leaving.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.520
<b>That Catcher's Got a Sharp Tongue</b>

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.010
<i>I leave the house at 6 AM.</i>

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.480
<i>It takes me 30 to 40 minutes to get
to Fuurin Middle School by bike.</i>

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.890
<i>In the beginning, it was rough,</i>

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.770
<i>but this low-impact aerobic exercise
is the perfect way to warm up.</i>

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.440
Wow, it's so early, but you're all here!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.540
Morning.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.290
You're late, Daigo.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.530
The first-years are coming today.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.850
We can't have the veterans slacking off.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.100
Where's Tanba-san?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.190
That figures.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.150
Hey, I don't mean to be a downer,

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:42.110
but do you really think those guys
are gonna show up to morning practice?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.030
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.030
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.150
Nishina-kun!

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.930
Oh, Senpai.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.380
G'morning.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.570
Don't "g'morning" me!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:00.750
What's your deal?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.300
I told you yesterday
we had morning practice today.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.340
You better have a good
reason for not coming!

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.620
Oh, my sincerest apologies. I overslept.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.350
As if! None of the first-years showed up!

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:16.310
Was shaking hands with
the captain yesterday all for show?!

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.930
I've had enough of you disrespecting us.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.120
You'll find no disrespect here.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.350
I'm even talking politely.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.750
That's totally not the issue!

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:32.180
We just want to work with
a proper coach, is all.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.500
We don't wanna risk getting injured
doing drills we can't trust.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.960
We won't be at afternoon practice, either.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.220
When Coach shows up, so will we.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.970
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.970
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.970
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.930
What? They're skipping
afternoon practice, too?

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.610
He said they'd only listen to their coach.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.690
Can you believe those jerks?

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.810
They're really pushing it...

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.770
So much for the cute little
first-year stereotype.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.880
Oh, well. If that's their reason,
forcing them won't do anything.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.740
We'll just practice by ourselves 
until this new coach shows up.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.450
You're so soft, Daigo.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.690
Is everyone here?

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.660
Tanba-san?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.620
Our adviser, Yamaguchi-sensei, 
wants to talk to us.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:13.870
Huh?

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.200
Is this everyone on the baseball team?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.630
And you're the captain?
What was your name again?

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.660
I-It's Shigeno.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.840
<i>She didn't remember my name.</i>

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:32.850
Well, uh, I haven't been your adviser long,

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.310
and I don't know all that
much about your team.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.770
However, I'm here to pass on some
urgent news from the principal.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:40.980
Urgent?

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.450
It seems Coach Kunimoto, who was
due to take over in the near future,

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.780
now won't be able to do so,
for various reasons.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:54.440
We intend to find an external 
replacement as quickly as possible,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.710
but until then, please try to train
the best you can on your own.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.840
Nanshou Monorail

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.840
Nanshou Monorail

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.840
Mifune Station

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.840
Mifune Station

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:07.840
No way.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.180
I can't believe this is happening.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.970
The only reason we even came to this school
is 'cause Coach was coming here, too.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.900
What the heck is all this now?!

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.520
God, shut up. As if we know...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.850
Chiba, you've got a smartphone.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:23.340
Call up Coach.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.030
Wh-Who, me?

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.560
Yes, you! Call him!

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.490
Seriously?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.920
And?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.010
Not picking up?

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.360
Uh, no...

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:43.340
It's saying this number is no longer in service...

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.340
That old geezer won't get away with this!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.550
He totally stabbed us in the back!

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.230
Who would've guessed our new coach 
would back out at the last minute?

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.150
They trusted their coach,
and he betrayed them...

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.730
I feel kinda sorry for those guys.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.900
They got what they deserved,

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.000
acting all arrogant like that.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.440
Serves them right.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:18.540
The problem is, they might just quit now.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:24.900
They won't. They came here
 on baseball scholarships.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.460
They're not gonna up and quit that easily.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:30.220
Daigo, look!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.410
There are people over there.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.640
Do you think they're here to join?

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.400
Chisato! Anita!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.810
Senpai!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.770
"Senpai"?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:50.740
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:50.740
<b>Fujii Chisato</b>

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.480
Fujii Chisato, a former Yokohama Little regular.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.740
She plays center field.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:57.240
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:57.240
<b>Tabashima Anita</b>

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:55.900
Tabashima Anita,
also a former Yokohama Little regular.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.240
She plays catcher.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.830
We used to be teammates,
but they joined after us.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:05.250
I told them to come play
middle school baseball with us,

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.160
instead of jumping to Senior Little League,
where the gap between boys and girls widens.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.350
Yes!

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:14.300
That's why we came here with big ambitions,
fixin' to give it our all!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.300
And since y'all are short on players,
we'll be starters in no time!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.160
I s-see...

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.770
A Kansai accent?

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:26.730
Anita moved here from Brazil in the 
fourth grade. Her father's from Kansai.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:29.570
I can definitely vouch for them.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.200
With those scholarship students too,
our team's getting quite a boost.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.720
<i>We now have thirteen on the team.</i>

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.450
<i>Tanba-san and I are guaranteed to get benched.</i>

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.450
Great!

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.210
We've got more girls than boys,
but we'll go far this year!

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.170
<i>You shouldn't be so happy!</i>

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.170
Hey, Anita, you play catcher, right?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.130
You were Yokohama Little's starting catcher?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.960
Yes.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:55.330
We went to the national quarters
with me playing catcher.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.090
I played cleanup, too.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.700
So who's yer starting catcher here?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.730
That would be me.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.730
My name's Shigeno Daigo.
I'm the captain and the catcher.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.080
Oh, boy.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.950
What'm I gonna do, Sawa-senpai?

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:19.620
I'm 100 percent taking the starting spot
away from the captain.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.560
How do I break it to him
without being offensive?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.910
Whatta bind!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.950
You're already being offensive, Anita.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.380
Talk about jumping the gun!
Let's not worry about that yet.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.660
There's another first-year who plays catcher, too.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.050
You can join practice tomorrow,
and we'll make the call eventually.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.290
You can just watch for today.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:47.330
Aw, shucks. The little
fella wriggled out of it.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.210
He don't look like much of a captain.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.570
Is he really up to it?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:52.700
I wonder...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:57.820
But he's captain ahead of Sawa-san and Sagara-san.
He must have something about him.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.560
I s'pose.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:03.950
Well, that starting catcher spot is mine.
I ain't lettin' him take it.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.790
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.790
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.790
What'd you say?!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.160
You're not joining the baseball team?!

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.240
Yeah.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.680
I talked it over with my family.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.800
We're going to play Senior League instead.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.530
Now, now, hold on a sec!

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.100
The school isn't gonna allow that.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.700
The whole reason we got accepted here was
on the condition we join the baseball team!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.270
Our grades aren't good enough.
They're not going to—

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.980
Speak for yourself.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:31.940
Huh?

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:33.940
You didn't know?

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.400
The four of us got in by passing
the regular entrance exam.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.860
You're the only one

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:43.520
who relied on the scholarship to get in
on a huge discount without passing an exam.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.950
Sorry, Nishina.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.920
But if Coach isn't coming,

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.320
we've got no reason to play baseball here.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.090
So, unfortunately,

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:05.270
all the first-year boys
 besides Nishina have quit.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.860
Six girls. Three boys.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:14.400
We barely have enough to field a team,
but let's do our best with the nine of us!

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.910
<i>You gotta be kidding me 
with this girl-infested team.</i>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:32.990
<i>Fine. I'll just show you how good I am during
training and take control of this team.</i>

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:39.910
One, two!

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:40.630
One, two!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.410
One, two!

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:42.010
One, two!

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.970
Two... three...

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.300
Drop down even further!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:57.500
Five... six... seven...

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.480
Okay, everyone, take five.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.420
Maybe this was a little too intense
for the first-years' first session.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:09.550
But you can tell Anita and Chisato
are from Yokohama Little.

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:12.400
You were able to keep up from the start.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:16.170
I don't believe it.
Y'all do this routine every day?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.270
A year ago, we weren't able to keep up, either.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:23.630
The physical difference between grade school
 and middle school is pretty huge.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:27.430
Speaking of, we got one 
ex-grade schooler dying over there.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.370
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.640
<i>There's no way I can keep up with this.</i>

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.520
Are you okay?

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.160
W-Water...

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.480
Give me...

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:42.750
Here you go.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.130
Wh-Wh-What the hell are you doing?!

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:49.090
Ah, that perked you right up.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.410
You surprised me, Nishina.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:55.520
I feel bad for you because it must be hard
without your coach and your friends.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.380
We're really grateful
you actually showed up to practice.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:00.980
We mean it.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.090
If you hadn't come,
we'd only have eight players.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:10.310
Pfft, I d-didn't come to help out you guys.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.720
All right.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:17.070
Infielders, outfielders, and the battery
 have separate drills,

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.230
so I'd like to settle
on a provisional lineup.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:24.190
Our candidates for pitcher 
are Mutsuko and Nishina.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.360
Since we only have nine players,

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.660
when you're not pitching,
you'll have to play outfield.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.250
For the infield, we've got Tanba-san on first.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.610
Sawa-san on second.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.080
Shortstop: Tao.

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:38.040
Third: Kandori.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.750
In the outfield, we've got
Chisato at center field.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.930
The catchers will be Anita and myself.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:50.090
Again, this is provisional,
 so these positions may change.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.050
But let's run with it for now—

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:54.060
Yo, hold up!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:58.030
What's all this ramblin' about
"provisional" this, "provisional" that?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:01.480
Well, maybe it'll work fine
for the <i>other</i> positions...

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.730
But we oughta nail down
who's the starting catcher

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:07.450
and who's the bullpen
catcher now, don'tcha think?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.660
Don't be so pushy, Anita.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:15.770
Daigo said yesterday we'd decide all that
once we see how practice goes.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.370
Why are you so worked up?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.180
You're right, I <i>am</i> worked up.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.800
We ain't got a coach,

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:25.260
so if our captain, Shigeno-senpai, 
makes himself the starting catcher,

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.590
ain't nothin' I can do about it!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:31.900
Besides, why're you takin' this fella's side?

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:32.890
What?

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:37.080
I always play baseball with the
intention of never losin' to a boy!

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:40.600
Any girl who sucks up to boys is my enemy, too!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.050
Excuse me?!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.560
<b>Excuse me?!</b>

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.660
Looks like Anita's illness 
is flaring up again.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.150
Who are you accusing of sucking up?!

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:52.610
Oh, boy. So there really are girls
who suck up without realizin'.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:56.200
How dare you! You don't 
know the first thing about me!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.200
<i>What's wrong with these two?</i>

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.540
All right, all right!

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:04.090
Okay, Anita, you can be our starting catcher.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.700
H-Hey, hold on, Daigo.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.990
You haven't even seen her play yet.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:18.290
Yeah, but if she was the starting catcher for
Yokohama Little, she's gotta be good, right?

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.680
And she's tall, too.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:25.170
I don't mind as long as
it makes the team stronger.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:29.610
I'm not gonna tie up a position just 
because I'm the captain and a senior.

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:33.080
Besides, since we don't have a coach,

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.580
I'll probably have my hands
full managing the team.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.890
I also have to oversee fielding
practice, so this works out great.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:43.310
Mutsuko, I'll leave battery 
practice to you and Anita.

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:48.710
Huh. Our captain ain't as dumb as he looks.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.870
All righty. Let's do this!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.180
I'm lookin' forward to this.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.970
Nice one, shortstop!

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.820
Next, 5-4-3!

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.770
Good job!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.830
Outfield, to center!

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:25.640
Nice one, Chisato!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.750
Her reading of the ball's
trajectory is impeccable.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.300
Senpai!

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.010
Put some mustard on the next one!

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.870
She's already pitching at full-speed, Anita.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.250
Wait, what?

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.130
That's yer best? For real?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.620
These gentle pitches
that nestle in the mitt?

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.240
How're you even a candidate for pitcher?!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.240
<b>Blush</b>

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.580
Sh-Shut up!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:58.000
I know it myself!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.930
It's not like I'm pitching because I want to!

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:04.710
We were short on players, so I ended up
pitching by process of elimination!

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.610
You ain't doin' it 'cause you want to?

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.140
What garbage is that?

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.670
If that's true, you should stop pitchin'.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:17.800
The most important thing for
a pitcher is here! Right here!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.890
Someone with no heart,
someone that unmotivated,

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.180
don't belong on the
highest point in the field.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.470
What? Are you serious right now?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:33.820
You think I'm going to let some
snot-nosed rookie lecture me?!

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.510
Screw this!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.410
Hey... What are you doing, Mutsuko?

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:45.850
I can't play with someone like her.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:47.370
I'm not pitching anymore!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.340
B-But why?

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.420
And let's not forget about <i>you</i>!

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.040
I've lost all respect for you.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.390
Disappointed!

00:17:58.520 --> 00:17:59.960
I'm going home for today!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.930
She went home...

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.830
Sakura, wanna have a go
at pitching tomorrow?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.640
Huh? Pitching?

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.590
Mutsuko?

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.290
Yes?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.920
Shigeno-kun is here.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.310
Should I send him up to your room?

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:36.260
What? N-No, no! I'll come out!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.040
Sorry for making you wait.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.760
I was just getting out of the bath.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.680
Oh, no problem.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.730
I'm sorry for just showing up like this.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:52.490
I was worried because you said you
were quitting pitching and left early.

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.940
Oh, Anita told me what your fight was about.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:57.900
O-Oh.

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:02.870
I ticked her off about it,
but she said she wasn't trying to be mean.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:07.760
She was just surprised because she got
used to catching some crazy fastballs

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:09.830
when she was with Yokohama Little.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.520
I-It's fine, really.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:18.510
I know she has no filter
because she was raised abroad.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:21.780
But well, she was right.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.470
I'm not built to be a pitcher.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.650
And we've got Nishina now.
I'll just go into the outfield—

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:31.130
That's not true.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.320
Nishina can't do it alone.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:38.820
On top of that, we need to develop him
slowly but surely for the future of the team.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.440
And, well, Anita hasn't
seen your good side yet.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:47.460
Once she does, I'm sure she'll change her mind.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.950
And if she doesn't,

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.920
she won't be our starting catcher.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:03.090
Anyway, I want you to have a proper 
training session with Anita tomorrow.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:07.120
An upperclassman can't throw
in the towel like you did today.

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:10.920
It's fine for you two to butt heads.

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:14.640
You need to communicate 
and understand each other.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:18.320
That's how it was with Hikaru and me.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.570
Batteries aren't made overnight.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:27.330
They're a partnership
you have to forge together.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:28.980
Yeah.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:30.770
Let's do our best.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.330
You got this, Mutsuko.

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:37.760
Thank you, Daigo.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.710
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.710
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:57.400
That's no good. Stop, stop!

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:02.090
You ain't got great control to begin with,

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:07.030
and after about thirty pitches,
your power and control fall apart completely.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:12.000
You moron. If all you got is fastballs for
the first few innings, yer useless in a game.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.010
I don't care if yer from a fancy club
or got in on a scholarship.

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.960
You hafta start over with the basics!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.990
You wanna say that again?!

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.380
Nishina, calm down!

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:25.160
What?! Let go of me!

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.340
You're pissed at her too, aren't you?!

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:30.060
Nope, not really.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.430
She's just giving us her honest
assessment as our catcher.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:37.560
So all we can do to shut her up
is pitch in a way she can't criticize.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.780
Anita, you ready to catch my pitches now?

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:45.770
Sure.

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:49.480
Hey, what's wrong?

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:50.700
Oh, uh, sorry.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.550
Shigeno-kun, do you have a moment?

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.370
Yamaguchi-sensei.

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.830
What is it?

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:04.420
Right. This is all new to me,
so I sort of forgot about this.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:08.700
I got this a while ago, but I overlooked it.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:15.980
<b>Kanagawa Prefecture Middle School Spring Season Preliminaries (Nippon Junior High School Physical Culture Association)</b>

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:15.980
<b>Prefecture East District Bracket</b>

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:15.980
<b>Final</b>

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:12.760
It looks like we were
entered for something called

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:16.640
the Kanagawa Prefecture Middle
School Spring Season Preliminaries.

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:21.280
The tournament is in two weeks.

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:23.820
Good for you.
You can play in actual games.

